{"content":[{"c":["BALAK"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["Zippor’s son, king of Moab. Balak became fearful after the Israelites defeated the Amorites, so he attempted to hire a soothsayer named Balaam to pronounce a curse against Israel (",{"href":"?bref=Num.22.1-7","r":"Num.22.1-7","rawR":"Num.22.1-7","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Num.22.1-7","value":"Num.22.1-7"}],"t":"ref","v":"Nm 22:1-7"},"). Balak escorted Balaam to three different mountains and offered three different sacrifices, only to have Balaam each time deliver a blessing to the Israelites (chs ",{"href":"?bref=Num.22.1-24.25","r":"Num.22.1-24.25","rawR":"Num.22.1-24.25","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Num.22.1-24.25","value":"Num.22.1-24.25"}],"t":"ref","v":"22–24"},"). Enraged, Balak sent Balaam away. That event was later remembered as an example of God’s special blessing on the Israelites and of the futility of trying to alter God’s will (",{"href":"?bref=Josh.24.9-10","r":"Josh.24.9-10","rawR":"Josh.24.9-10","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Josh.24.9-10","value":"Josh.24.9-10"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jos 24:9-10"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Judg.11.25","r":"Judg.11.25","rawR":"Judg.11.25","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Judg.11.25","value":"Judg.11.25"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jgs 11:25"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Mic.6.5","r":"Mic.6.5","rawR":"Mic.6.5","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Mic.6.5","value":"Mic.6.5"}],"t":"ref","v":"Mi 6:5"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Rev.2.14","r":"Rev.2.14","rawR":"Rev.2.14","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Rev.2.14","value":"Rev.2.14"}],"t":"ref","v":"Rv 2:14"},")."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"},{"c":[{"c":["See also"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," ",{"href":"?item=Balaam_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"Balaam_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"Balaam_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Balaam"},"."],"sourceClass":"","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Balak","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Nm 22:1-7","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Num.22.1-7","rawQueryValue":"Num.22.1-7","sourceRefExact":"Num.22.1-7"},{"anchorText":"22–24","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Num.22.1-24.25","rawQueryValue":"Num.22.1-24.25","sourceRefExact":"Num.22.1-24.25"},{"anchorText":"Jos 24:9-10","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Josh.24.9-10","rawQueryValue":"Josh.24.9-10","sourceRefExact":"Josh.24.9-10"},{"anchorText":"Jgs 11:25","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Judg.11.25","rawQueryValue":"Judg.11.25","sourceRefExact":"Judg.11.25"},{"anchorText":"Mi 6:5","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Mic.6.5","rawQueryValue":"Mic.6.5","sourceRefExact":"Mic.6.5"},{"anchorText":"Rv 2:14","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Rev.2.14","rawQueryValue":"Rev.2.14","sourceRefExact":"Rev.2.14"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"2304f360721a7ee8d02425517677b37da748a5f0f48065e09e14b8d2283a985f","sourceItemName":"Balak","sourceItemOrder":52,"sourceMember":"Articles/B.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Balak","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Balak","title":"Balak","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}